# Race-condition experiment

## Hypothesis
Two threads incrementing the same counter without synchronization can lose updates.

## Evidence
Expected: 200000
Actual: 100087

## Conclusion
`counter = counter + 1` is a read-modify-write sequence, not an atomic operation.
The unsynchronized version has a C++ data race; an occasional correct result would not prove safety.

## Mutex version
A mutex protects the counter's read-modify-write invariant, so the final count is 200000.